+**Current cross-engine transfer limit (WP28).** Workspace warp refuses any family with an owner-only fence or any durable guest input before its first network request. Current workspace history/live replication sends a restriction-only `x-vector-session-replication: 1` marker: the source refuses histories containing either restriction and withholds restricted live envelopes at emission. Ordinary owner reads and live UI events remain available, and local archives preserve their restrictive provenance. This stops future private bytes; it cannot revoke public snapshots a peer received before fencing. A restriction-aware replication protocol is required before these families can move between engines. Older clients without the replication marker cannot be distinguished from ordinary owner reads and have no private-transfer guarantee.
